  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 345 AM CDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nThe extended forecast remains rather pedestrian, as most of the \nnoteworthy changes are frontloaded into the short term.  By Sunday \nafternoon, the upper ridge over SoCal is forecast to meander \neastward to the Four Corners, nudging the upper trough east.  This \nwill result in a gradual increase in thicknesses/temperatures \nthrough midweek or so, when highs top out Wednesday afternoon ~ 7-9 \nF above normal.  Despite this increase, highs will still be in the \n80s most locations.  Absent any triggers in the synoptic pattern, as \nwell as cold fronts, rain chances will be hard to come by, and \nrestricted away from the ridge to the mountains in the south.  Even \nso, chances remain minimal.",
